      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "When circumstances feel completely predetermined, the desire to simply stop fighting is a very natural response to mounting pain. Perhaps the \"point\" isn't about changing the ultimate outcome, but about preserving your own well-being and dignity *while* the difficult period lasts. Enduring doesn't always mean passively accepting destruction; it can also mean finding small pockets of peace or connection amidst the chaos.",
      "source": "target",
